# Sentinel — canonical publication policy state.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE STATE `scripts/check-rename-gate.sh` JUDGES AGAINST, and it is
# deliberately a tracked repository artifact rather than an environment variable. A change
# of publication policy has to appear in a diff and be reviewable by someone who was not in
# the room; an export in one operator's shell is neither, and it evaporates. The guard that
# reads this file refuses to run without it.
#
# IT DOES NOT AUTHORISE ANYTHING BY ITSELF. It records what the project's expected
# publication state IS, so that a machine can notice the day reality stops matching it.
# Editing this file is not permission to publish; it is a declaration that permission was
# given elsewhere, and the guard checks that the elsewhere exists.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FORMAT
#
# Blank lines and lines whose first character is `#` are ignored. EVERY other line must be
# exactly `KEY=VALUE`: no surrounding spaces, no quotes, no `export`, no substitution, no
# carriage returns. The guard PARSES this file line by line; it never sources it, because a
# policy artifact that can execute code is not a policy artifact.
#
# Unknown keys, duplicate keys, missing keys, empty values, and unrecognised values all make
# the guard REFUSE. That is the project's zero-value principle applied to its own
# configuration: an unset or damaged state reads as refusal, never as permission.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KEYS
#
# PUBLICATION_STATE      HELD_PRIVATE | AUTHORIZED_PUBLIC
#
#   HELD_PRIVATE       — the default and the current state. Every configured GitHub remote
#                        must read PRIVATE. One found public is a hard failure, immediately,
#                        on whichever run notices it first.
#   AUTHORIZED_PUBLIC  — a public transition has been authorised. This value is NOT
#                        reachable by editing one word: it additionally requires a resolved
#                        RIGHTS_MODE and a SMITH_DECISION reference that is actually recorded
#                        in `docs/decisions.md`, and it requires this file to be committed.
#
# RIGHTS_MODE            UNDECIDED | OPEN_SOURCE | PROPRIETARY | SOURCE_AVAILABLE
#
#   OPEN_SOURCE is the current value: Apache-2.0, ruled by John at D-097 (2026-09-04), with
#   `LICENSE` and `NOTICE` at the repository root. ~~UNDECIDED was a DELIBERATE HOLD (D-082(c))~~
#   until that ruling; no agent selected it. UNDECIDED remains legal while HELD_PRIVATE and a
#   CONTRADICTION under AUTHORIZED_PUBLIC — you cannot authorise publication of a work whose
#   terms of use nobody has chosen.
#
# SMITH_DECISION         NONE | a recorded decision reference
#
#   `NONE` while held. Under AUTHORIZED_PUBLIC it must be a `D-NNN` decision-log id or an
#   `S-YYYYMMDD-...` session id, AND the guard greps `docs/decisions.md` for it. A reference
#   to a ruling nobody wrote down is not a ruling.
#
# CANONICAL_REPOSITORY   host/owner/name
#
#   The repository this policy is ABOUT. The guard normalises every configured remote URL
#   and requires one of them to resolve to this value, so that it can state it is judging
#   the repository it thinks it is rather than whatever remote it happened to find. Every
#   OTHER configured GitHub remote is inspected too — the point of the census is that a
#   second remote added later must not slip past a guard hardcoded to `origin`.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CURRENT STATE, ruled by John on 2026-08-30 and transcribed as D-082(b)/(c). Publication is
# not authorised. Gate 8 passed with limits under D-080, and D-048 makes a clean result a
# precondition rather than a trigger. ~~The licence is deliberately held~~ — resolved to
# Apache-2.0 at D-097 (2026-09-04); the rights mode below records it. Publication is still a
# separate ruling and SMITH_DECISION stays NONE until it is made.

PUBLICATION_STATE=HELD_PRIVATE
RIGHTS_MODE=OPEN_SOURCE
SMITH_DECISION=NONE
CANONICAL_REPOSITORY=github.com/johnrfite1/sentinel
